7898776,2023-11-24,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"Negative Items : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX  Experian XXXX XXXX XXXX - XXXX "" Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act, specifically 15 USC 1681 section 602 ( a ), it is emphasized that consumer reporting agencies, such as XXXX and Experian, have a significant responsibility to handle consumer information with fairness, impartiality, and respect for privacy rights. As a consumer, I have the right to ensure that my private information is not shared, as supported by 15 USC 6801, which states that financial institutions must actively uphold customer privacy and safeguard nonpublic personal information.

According to 15 USC 1681 section 604 ( a ) ( 2 ), consumer reporting agencies, including XXXX and Experian, are only allowed to furnish a consumer report when provided with written instructions from the consumer. As the consumer, I have not provided any written consent for these agencies or the financial institution involved ( referred to as "" Furnisher of information to credit agencies '' ) to share my information. Therefore, any form of consent given to XXXX, Experian, or the financial institution, including verbal, non-verbal, written, implied, or otherwise, is now revoked. 

Additionally, as per 15 USC 6802 ( b ) ( c ), a financial institution can not disclose nonpublic personal information to a nonaffiliated third party without informing the consumer of their option to exercise nondisclosure. However, the "" Furnisher of information to credit agencies '' did not inform me of this right. This is a violation of my rights.

Furthermore, according to 15 USC 1681C ( a ) ( 5 ), unless authorized under subsection ( b ), no consumer reporting agency can include any adverse item of information in a consumer report, except for records of convictions that are more than XXXX years old. The account being reported without my permission is considered an adverse item. 

In conclusion, XXXX and Experian, as consumer reporting agencies, along with the financial institution ( "" Furnisher of information to credit agencies '' ), do not have my consent to furnish this information, and they have failed to provide me with necessary notifications regarding my rights. Furthermore, the reporting of adverse information without proper authorization violates the regulations stated in the Fair Credit Reporting Act. ''",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,Experian Information Solutions Inc.,TX,75604,,Web,2023-11-24,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
