The FCRA mandates that credit reporting agencies must ensure the maximum possible accuracy of the information they report. The continued misreporting of my closed child support account, along with the discrepancy in the name associated with the account, constitutes a clear violation of these regulations. 

I have previously attempted to resolve this matter by contacting XXXX, Equifax and XXXX directly and have disputed this account, highlighting its inaccuracies and requesting its removal. Despite these efforts, the account continues to be reported, demonstrating a failure on their part to adequately investigate and rectify the inaccuracies in my credit report. 

